# ARTSA — AI Containment Platform Context

## Product
Enterprise cybersecurity dashboard for real-time AI agent containment, escape detection, and red-team wargaming. Not a generic SaaS template — prioritize security UX clarity over decorative UI.

## Stack
| Layer | Tech |
|-------|------|
| Frontend | Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, Recharts |
| Backend | FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy async, pytest |
| AI | LangChain provider registry, LLM judge, embedding-based semantic detection |

## Repo layout
- `frontend/` — Next.js command center (port 3000)
- `backend/src/api/` — production containment API (port 8000 via uvicorn)
- `api-gateway/` — wargame/campaign gateway (separate app)
- Do not conflate the two port-8000 apps without explicit user request

## Frontend pages (preserve functionality)
`/`, `/observatory`, `/wargame`, `/attack-library`, `/providers`, `/reports`, `/topology`, `/replay`, `/xray`

## API contracts — do not change unless asked
- Containment: `/api/v1/ingest`, `/metrics/dashboard`, `/observatory`, `/topology`, `/websocket`
- Gateway: `/api/v1/campaigns/run`, `/attack-library`
- Use `fetchFromBackend()` and existing env `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`

## UX priorities
1. Live telemetry visibility (WebSocket + polling fallback)
2. Severity-at-a-glance (critical/high/medium/low)
3. Sub-50ms containment SLO messaging where relevant
4. Dark theme, premium density, accessible contrast

## Code generation defaults
- Match existing naming: `ContainmentEngine`, `SeverityBadge`, `fetchFromBackend`
- Prefer extending detectors/routes over parallel implementations
- Keep mock fallbacks when API offline (graceful degradation)
